# Pre-auth connection limits (O200; server/README.md "Pre-auth connection limits (O200)").
# The stock engine accepts any number of connections and keeps each one for CONNECTION_READ_TIMEOUT (30 s) before it has
# said a word; its only throttle (Ban::acceptConnection) stops 6 connections of one IP within 500 ms. A few hundred idle
# sockets from one host held the file descriptors and the io threads' attention. Now (all keys in config.lua, 0 = off):
#   * src/chaospreauth.h (new, header only, no engine types; server/tools/chaospreauth_test.cpp tests it): a table of the
#     connections that have not logged in yet. Per IP at most preAuthMaxPerIp (5), in all preAuthMaxTotal (200); an IP
#     opening more than preAuthRateMax (10) connections within preAuthRateWindow (10) seconds is refused for
#     preAuthCooldown (30) seconds. Refused connections are closed at once, before any packet is read. The table is
#     bounded (100,000 IPs; expired ones are swept) and behind one mutex; one console line per kind per 10 s:
#     [Pre-auth limit] ... : ip (N more refused since the last line).
#   * ServicePort::onConnectionReady counts the connection (before the old throttle, so a flood never reaches the ban
#     list). Exempt, not counted: 127.0.0.0/8 (preAuthExemptLoopback = true: the admin tools, the watchdog, the health
#     check) and the trusted gateways of patch 0025 (their clients are counted by their own address, from the PROXY
#     header). The login (7171), game (7172) and status ports all count: one connection of any of them is one.
#   * Connection: startPreAuth arms a deadline timer (preAuthDeadline, 15 s): a connection that has not logged in by then
#     is closed. endPreAuth gives the count back and cancels the timer; it runs on every close path (close(), also a
#     repeated one, and the destructor) and when a game login went through (ProtocolGame::login / ::connect), under the
#     connection's lock and once per connection (a flag), so nothing leaks and nothing is given back twice. A login or
#     status connection ends by closing, a game connection by its login.
#   * not covered: the live cast port (chaoscastserver.cpp has its own acceptor and limits).
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0066: patch -p1 < 0067-preauth-limits.patch, then rebuild.
new file mode 100644
